From d0363d8b096eb0fdef686a7822189bcd90ea59b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 12:31:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/40] feat(sling): capture cwd/beads-dir/stderr on bd mol
 bond failure (gfork-i3d diagnostics)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`gt sling`'s `bd mol bond` can fail to resolve a bead as its second operand
("'<bead>' not found") while `bd show` still resolves it — a live stale-read /
wrong-database condition that surfaced only as a bare "exit status 1", hiding
which database bd actually consulted. Capture bd's stderr and record the working
directory, the resolved .beads database, and the exact argv in the wrapped error
for both the primary wisp->bead bond and the direct-formula fallback, so the
next recurrence is diagnosable instead of guessed.

This is instrumentation, not a fix: gfork-i3d stays open pending a live
recurrence with these diagnostics. AllowStale() is deliberately NOT wired onto
the mol-bond read — its flag permits stale reads, the wrong direction for a
stale-read bug.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
